  "_comment": "Finite lexicon for the en-US passive detector. The detector is productive: any word ending in -ed after a form of 'be' is a candidate participle, so recall does not depend on a list. The lists below only (1) add a finite, registered list of irregular past participles — English participles are not a closed class, so an irregular participle missing from the list is not detected, (2) remove -ed words that are not participles, (3) remove participles that after 'be' overwhelmingly name a state rather than an action, and (4) recognise a 'by' that introduces a time, means or manner instead of an agent. Lists (3) and (4) trade recall for precision and are declared limitations. Compiled for Lucid from the principal parts of English irregular verbs and from US federal plain-language register; no frequency list is used.",
